  "conditionalPinCrestDesignNotImplemented": {
    "status": "Not recommended as the next product version merely because it is a small change; retained only as a falsifiable design option.",
    "systemDesign": [
      "Retain current rest/index carrier, gains, protected domains and front system.",
      "For mouth-up only, remove currently free semantic crest IDs from unknowns and impose deltaUp=0 by Dirichlet elimination.",
      "Keep original coordinates in RHS neighbour differences; fixed crest delta contributes zero. Rebuild the up free-index mapping, never zero solved crest entries after solving.",
      "The reduced up matrix is a principal submatrix of the existing SPD matrix. Preserve PCG residual checks, whole-proposal cap and triangle guards.",
      "Report per-component free counts and crest constraint-mask hash. Matched current binding would have 3848 front unknowns and 3714 up unknowns after removing 134 free crest vertices; calculate rather than hardcode."
    ],
    "nativeStageCaveat": "写入前的 crest up 约束可以精确；之后原生微几何沿改变后的法线运行，最终 crest 仍须独立测量，不可宣称最终原图轮廓精确。",
    "whyNotEnough": "该约束最多先取消收缩的一部分，混合带另一端可能同步移动，尖转也可能重集中在锚点一环。没有证据使其足以满足明显改善。"
  },
  "falsificationConditionsForAnyFutureGeometryCandidate": [
    "Original-size jaw front, jaw oblique and speak beauty still read as the same narrow hard edge, even if angle/residual/displacement metrics improve.",
    "The semantic crest is held but shoulder outer endpoint movement still shrinks its visible or potential projected extent.",
    "Full connected path shows an equal or larger new concentrated turn at the constrained crest or neighbouring ring.",
    "Apparent gain depends on hiding lower teeth, reducing aperture/action, swelling the outer lip, or forcing the inner wall toward the chosen camera.",
    "Final inherited microgeometry changes protected native body/contact/non-skin positions, despite a locally valid intermediate proposal.",
    "Intermediate pose samples add ridges, dents or abrupt bands; neutral/pucker or real saves/restore/historical comparison regress."
  ],
